//@version=5
// V20 INDICATOR -- the same rules as V20_DONCHIAN_LINREG_strategy.pine, drawn on the chart.
//
// It plots the Donchian entry and exit channels, the 50-period linear regression, the entry window,
// and a marker on every bar the strategy would take -- with the stop and target it would place, so
// the levels can be read before the trade rather than after it. Alerts fire on the same condition.
//
// ================================ WHAT THE MEASUREMENTS SAY ================================
// This is not a recommendation to trade the plot. On five markets at two timeframes the rules below
// have NO demonstrable edge: bootstrap P(mean daily R <= 0) runs 0.41 to 0.97 on the locked block,
// every market turns negative at 1.5x the assumed spread, and the two long histories -- 8.5 years of
// US30 and 22 years of gold -- are negative or zero.
//
// THE REGRESSION IS REDUNDANT WITH THE TRIGGER, and its most literal reading is backwards. Share of
// bars passing each confirmation, US30 15m:
//
//   reading                    all bars   BREAKOUT bars    lift
//   slope > 0                     53.1%          78.2%    1.47x
//   forecast > close              50.5%          12.1%    0.24x   <- rejects breakouts
//   close > value                 49.7%          89.1%    1.80x   <- passes 89% of them
//   slope>0 AND close>value       21.8%          67.7%    3.11x
//
// On a breakout bar the regression's one-bar-ahead forecast sits BELOW the current price 88% of the
// time, because the bar has just jumped above the range the line is fitted to. The reading that
// scores best passes 89.1% of breakout bars, so it removes about a ninth of the trades and adds
// +0.005 R. Full numbers in docs/ib/STUDY_V20_LINREG.md.
//
// Two things the same measurements DO support: turning the take profit OFF (locked EV -0.008 ->
// +0.158 on US100, -0.002 -> +0.156 on gold, +0.016 -> +0.099 on NQ), and starting the session at
// the 09:30 cash open rather than before it -- every window beginning at 09:30 is pooled-positive
// and every window beginning earlier is not.
// ================================ ADX vs CHOP, MEASURED ================================
// A 110-cell ADX x CHOP grid on this base, five markets, pooled in R. The population first: 22% of
// cells have profit factor > 1 on research and 36% on locked, and the correlation between a cell's
// research PF and its locked PF is **+0.035** -- so a ranking of this grid should not transfer.
//
//   family        cells   research PF   LOCKED PF   % of cells with PF>1 on locked
//   ADX alone        10         0.959       0.961                10%
//   CHOP alone        9         0.965       0.986                44%
//   both             90         0.969       0.981                39%
//   no filter         1         0.959       0.968                 0%
//
// CHOP's ladder is monotone on BOTH blocks -- ceiling 100/55/50/45/40/35 gives research
// 0.959/0.965/0.992/1.007/1.029/1.027 and locked 0.968/0.971/0.986/1.022/1.015/1.044. ADX's is
// flat: every floor from 10 to 40 sits between 0.911 and 0.977 on research and 0.951 and 1.025 on
// locked.
//
// AGAINST A RANDOM FILTER OF THE SAME SELECTIVITY -- the only null a restrictive condition cannot
// beat by being restrictive:
//
//   filter             research p   LOCKED p
//   ADX >= 25              0.248      0.372     nothing
//   ADX >= 40              0.736      0.269     nothing
//   CHOP <= 50             0.003      0.133
//   **CHOP <= 45**         0.005      0.015     <- the only setting clearing BOTH blocks
//   CHOP <= 40             0.005      0.108
//   CHOP <= 35             0.041      0.083
//   ADX>=25 + CHOP<=35     0.040      0.215     <- ADX makes CHOP WORSE out of sample
//   ADX>=18 + CHOP<=35     0.016      0.127
//
// WHY ADX FAILS AND CHOP DOES NOT, mechanically: on US30 breakout bars ADX >= 25 passes 55.6%
// against 50.0% of bars in general -- a lift of **1.11x**, so it barely discriminates. CHOP <= 40
// passes 41.1% against 21.3% -- a lift of **1.93x**. And 68.3% of the bars CHOP keeps already pass
// ADX, so stacking them removes little that CHOP has not already removed.
//
// Against the harder minute-of-day matched control, CHOP <= 40 clears BOTH blocks only on US30
// (p 0.016 research, 0.039 locked; CHOP <= 35 gives 0.010 and 0.001). On US100, NQ, the 8.5-year
// US30 history and gold, research passes and the holdout does not. So: CHOP is a real filter and
// ADX is not, but "real" here means it clears a selectivity null broadly and a drift-priced null on
// one market of five.
//
// ==========================================================================================

indicator("V20 Donchian 30/20 + linear regression [signals]", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 200)

gE       = "Entry"
donLen   = input.int(30, "Donchian breakout length", minval = 2, group = gE)
useLong  = input.bool(true,  "Long signals", group = gE)
useShort = input.bool(false, "Short signals", group = gE,
     tooltip="Off by default: the short mirror of this family loses on every market measured, and every sample here is a rising one.")

gR       = "Linear regression confirmation"
lrLen    = input.int(50, "Regression length", minval = 5, group = gR,
     tooltip="Inert. 20/30/50/75/100 give pooled EV -0.029/-0.030/-0.024/-0.021/-0.019 across five markets.")
lrMode   = input.string("close>value", "Confirmation", options = ["off", "slope", "forecast", "close>value", "both"], group = gR,
     tooltip="forecast: only 12.1% of breakout bars pass this -- it mostly REJECTS breakouts. close>value: passes 89.1% of them and adds +0.005 R.")

gRg      = "Regime filter -- CHOP earns its place, ADX does not"
useChop  = input.bool(false, "Require CHOP(14) below a ceiling", group = gRg,
     tooltip="CHOP <= 45 is the only regime setting that beats a random filter of the same selectivity on BOTH blocks (p 0.005 research, 0.015 locked). The pooled profit factor ladder is monotone on both: 100 -> 0.959/0.968, 50 -> 0.992/0.986, 45 -> 1.007/1.022, 40 -> 1.029/1.015, 35 -> 1.027/1.044.")
chopMax  = input.float(45, "  CHOP ceiling", minval = 1, maxval = 100, step = 1, group = gRg)
useAdx   = input.bool(false, "Require ADX(14) above a floor", group = gRg,
     tooltip="OFF because it does nothing. Every ADX floor from 10 to 40 fails a same-selectivity control on both blocks (p 0.248 and 0.372 at 25). On breakout bars ADX >= 25 has a lift of 1.11x -- it barely discriminates. Adding it ON TOP of CHOP makes the holdout WORSE: CHOP<=35 alone p 0.083, with ADX>=25 p 0.215.")
adxMin   = input.float(25, "  ADX floor", minval = 0, step = 1, group = gRg)

gT       = "Trading window"
useWin   = input.bool(false, "Restrict signals to a session", group = gT)
winSess  = input.session("0930-1100", "Entry session, New York time", group = gT,
     tooltip="Best of seven tested (pooled -0.0179 -> +0.0345) and inconsistent underneath: it helps NQ and gold and hurts US30 and US100. A candidate, not a finding.")

gX       = "Levels"
atrLen   = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 2, group = gX,
     tooltip="ATR here is ema(TR, n), NOT ta.atr -- ta.atr is Wilder's RMA and a different series.")
stopMult = input.float(2.0, "ATR stop multiple", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = gX)
exitCh   = input.int(20, "Donchian exit channel", minval = 2, group = gX)
useTp    = input.bool(true, "Show a take profit", group = gX,
     tooltip="Turning this off is the single change the measurements support.")
tpR      = input.float(2.0, "  target, in R", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = gX)
showLv   = input.bool(true, "Draw the stop and target of the last signal", group = gX)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- series
atrN    = ta.ema(ta.tr(true), atrLen)
entHi   = ta.highest(high, donLen)[1]    // ENTRY channels exclude this bar so a break is possible
entLo   = ta.lowest(low,  donLen)[1]
exLo    = ta.lowest(low,  exitCh)
exHi    = ta.highest(high, exitCh)

// ta.linreg(source, n, 0) is the fitted value AT the current bar. The slope is that value minus the
// same fit one bar back; the one-bar-ahead forecast is the value plus the slope. Verified against
// an explicit least-squares fit to 1e-6 in research/v20/v20linreg.py.
lrVal   = ta.linreg(close, lrLen, 0)
lrSlope = lrVal - ta.linreg(close, lrLen, 1)
lrFc    = lrVal + lrSlope

okLongC  = lrMode == "off" ? true : lrMode == "slope" ? lrSlope > 0 :
     lrMode == "forecast" ? lrFc > close : lrMode == "close>value" ? close > lrVal :
     (lrSlope > 0 and close > lrVal)
okShortC = lrMode == "off" ? true : lrMode == "slope" ? lrSlope < 0 :
     lrMode == "forecast" ? lrFc < close : lrMode == "close>value" ? close < lrVal :
     (lrSlope < 0 and close < lrVal)

// BARE `hour`/`minute` ARE EXCHANGE TIME IN PINE -- Chicago for CME, an hour off New York.
inWin = not useWin or not na(time(timeframe.period, winSess, "America/New_York"))
// CHOP(14) = 100 * log10(sum(TR,14) / (14-bar range)) / log10(14). LOW means trending.
chopV  = 100 * math.log10(math.sum(ta.tr(true), 14) /
     math.max(ta.highest(high, 14) - ta.lowest(low, 14), syminfo.mintick)) / math.log10(14)
[_p2, _m2, adxV] = ta.dmi(14, 14)        // returns [+DI, -DI, ADX] IN THAT ORDER
regimeOk = (not useChop or (not na(chopV) and chopV <= chopMax))
     and (not useAdx or (not na(adxV) and adxV >= adxMin))

ready = not na(atrN) and atrN > 0 and not na(lrVal)

// SIGNALS ARE CONFIRMED-BAR ONLY. Without `barstate.isconfirmed` a marker appears and disappears as
// the bar ticks, and an alert fires on a bar that never satisfied the rule at its close.
sigL = useLong  and ready and inWin and regimeOk and okLongC  and not na(entHi) and high > entHi and barstate.isconfirmed
sigS = useShort and ready and inWin and regimeOk and okShortC and not na(entLo) and low  < entLo and barstate.isconfirmed

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- the levels a signal implies
// The strategy enters at the NEXT bar's open, so these are drawn from the signal bar's close as an
// estimate. The real fill is one bar later and the stop is measured from it.
var float lastStop = na
var float lastTgt  = na
var int   lastDir  = 0

if sigL
    lastDir  := 1
    lastStop := math.max(close - stopMult * atrN, na(exLo) ? close - stopMult * atrN : math.min(exLo, close))
    lastStop := math.min(lastStop, close)
    lastTgt  := useTp ? close + tpR * stopMult * atrN : na
else if sigS
    lastDir  := -1
    lastStop := math.min(close + stopMult * atrN, na(exHi) ? close + stopMult * atrN : math.max(exHi, close))
    lastStop := math.max(lastStop, close)
    lastTgt  := useTp ? close - tpR * stopMult * atrN : na

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- plots
plot(useLong  ? entHi : na, "Donchian entry high", color = color.new(color.teal, 25), linewidth = 2)
plot(useShort ? entLo : na, "Donchian entry low",  color = color.new(color.maroon, 25), linewidth = 2)
plot(exLo, "Exit channel low",  color = color.new(color.gray, 55))
plot(exHi, "Exit channel high", color = color.new(color.gray, 55))
plot(lrVal, "Linear regression", color = color.new(color.orange, 0), linewidth = 2)
plot(lrMode == "forecast" ? lrFc : na, "Regression forecast (+1 bar)",
     color = color.new(color.yellow, 30), style = plot.style_circles)

plot(showLv and lastDir != 0 ? lastStop : na, "Stop of last signal",
     color = color.new(color.fuchsia, 20), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(showLv and lastDir != 0 and useTp ? lastTgt : na, "Target of last signal",
     color = color.new(color.lime, 20), style = plot.style_linebr)

plotshape(sigL, "Long signal", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar,
     color = color.new(color.teal, 0), size = size.small)
plotshape(sigS, "Short signal", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar,
     color = color.new(color.maroon, 0), size = size.small)

bgcolor(useWin and inWin ? color.new(color.teal, 94) : na, title = "entry window")

alertcondition(sigL, "V20 long signal",
     "V20: Donchian {{ticker}} up-break with the regression confirming, on {{interval}}")
alertcondition(sigS, "V20 short signal",
     "V20: Donchian {{ticker}} down-break with the regression confirming, on {{interval}}")

var table hud = table.new(position.top_right, 1, 3, border_width = 1)
if barstate.islast
    table.cell(hud, 0, 0, "V20 signals - NO demonstrable edge: bootstrap p 0.41 to 0.97, dies at 1.5x spread",
         text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.red, 20))
    table.cell(hud, 0, 1, lrMode == "forecast" ? "'forecast' passes only 12.1% of breakout bars - it rejects them" : lrMode == "off" ? "Confirmation OFF - this is the bare breakout" : "The regression passes ~89% of breakout bars and adds +0.005 R",
         text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.orange, 20))
    table.cell(hud, 0, 2, "Supported by the data: take profit OFF, and a session starting at 09:30 not before",
         text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 30))
